// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Noor Haddad, a freelance UX researcher in Houston, 2026-01-01 .. 2026-06-30. Hours become invoices, miles are
// measures, part of the apartment is her office, estimated tax is paid four times a year (three of them here), and one
// client is on a retainer. Cash basis, a sole proprietorship, no payroll.
//
// Written against PROPOSAL §6 and ASSOCIATIONS.md.   ✗ cannot say  ✎ says it badly  ? unclear  ⇄ sync  ▸ derived
// Ids: fl-c01 is freelancer, c = cannot say, 01; [A3] is the change in REPORT.md that closes it. Every balance is a
// replay of the lines below; the 2026 mileage rate and the safe-harbor figures are illustrative.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

base USD
use us
use us/tx
use us/401k
use us/se                 // self-employment tax, the QBI deduction, the safe harbor for estimates (a sketch)

entity noor : person
  born    1990-09-04
  filing  single
  lives   us/tx

/// The business: nothing but her, as a taxpayer sees it. What it earns and spends reaches her return on Schedule C.
entity noor-consulting : sole-proprietorship
  owner noor

param mileage-rate
  2026 0.725 USD/MI       // verify against the IRS notice

// ── who she works for: an engagement is a relator, and a retainer is one that is invoiced ────────────────

entity halcyon, northwind, kestrel, devconf : client

contract halcyon-retainer : engagement
  provider noor-consulting
  client halcyon
  4_500.00 USD monthly on 1 invoiced due 15d      // ✗ fl-c01 [A3] a retainer is an invoice from the day it is issued: v4 makes a claim only when a due day is missed (§7), so until then `claims` and `available` do not see it. FINDINGS proposal 1's `invoiced` is not in LANGUAGE.md
  includes 30 HR
  overage 150.00 USD/HR                           // billed on the next invoice: hours worked beyond the 30, by the `worked` lines
contract northwind : engagement
  provider noor-consulting
  client northwind
  140.00 USD/HR monthly on last invoiced due 30d  // the month's hours, by code
  // kestrel's fixed fee, 9,000.00 in three milestones, and the conference workshop are one-off claims, written below

// ── the apartment: a lease whose `uses` is a weighted many-slot ───────────────────────────────────────

contract apartment-rent : lease
  tenant noor
  landlord oak-court
  1_950.00 USD monthly on 1 from checking #rent
  uses noor 880 SQFT, noor-consulting 120 SQFT    // [A4] one slot with weights replaces `area` and `share 120 SQFT for studio`; 12% of the rent and of the utilities is the business's
contract coworking
  250.00 USD monthly on 3 from checking
contract health-insurance with blue-shield
  540.00 USD monthly on 5 from checking #premium
contract software
  129.00 USD monthly on 8 from checking
  share 100% for noor-consulting
contract phone with mint
  45.00 USD monthly on 10 from checking
  share 60% for noor-consulting

// ── positions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

entity chase : bank
  noor/checking : deposit
  noor/savings  : deposit
entity fidelity : broker
  noor/solo-401k                                  // ? fl-u02 [A1] her own plan: sponsor and participant are the same entity, in two slots of one relator
    sponsor noor-consulting
    monthly on 28 from checking deferral 1_500.00 USD

/// 30% of what arrives moves to savings and is held for the year's taxes. A budget `of income`: v5 §6.3 drops the
/// `#income` root the v4 form (`30% of #income`) used.
budget tax-reserve 30% of income monthly funded from checking into savings    // ✎ fl-b07 [open] §6.3 removed the root a budget limit was a share of; "everything that arrived" has no name

entity oak-court : landlord
entity blue-shield : health-insurer
entity mint : phone-company
entity delta, hotel-lumen, apple, ledger-cpa, hiscox : merchant

opening 2025-12-31
  checking          12_840.55 USD
  savings            9_600.00 USD
  noor/solo-401k    41_200.00 USD
  northwind owes noor 5_040.00 USD due 01-30 ^inv-nw-2512


2026-01

01 apartment-rent                                                  // ▸ 1,950.00 USD #rent of apartment, from checking; 12% (120 of 1,000 sqft) is the office's
01 halcyon-retainer                                                // ▸ halcyon owes noor 4,500.00 USD due 01-16 (net 15): income when it is paid, her books are cash

03 coworking                                                       // ▸ 250.00 USD

05 health-insurance                                                // ▸ 540.00 USD #premium: above the line, for the self-employed

08 software                                                        // ▸ 129.00 USD

10 phone                                                           // ▸ 45.00 USD, 60% of it the business's

14 checking <- halcyon 4_500.00 USD ^inv-hr-2601

15 checking -> irs 5_400.00 USD #estimated-tax for 2025            // ✎ fl-b06 [A6] the January installment belongs to the year before

20 noor worked 6.5 HR for northwind #research                      // ⇄ fl-s20 time tracker: one line per day, `worked`; the invoice bills the sum by its code

28 solo-401k                                                       // ▸ 1,500.00 USD elective deferral from checking into noor/solo-401k (no payroll: she is her own employer and employee)

29 checking <- northwind 5_040.00 USD ^inv-nw-2512                 // ▸ settles the opening invoice

31 car used 88 MI #business-travel                                 // ▸ 63.80 USD at 0.725 USD/MI (param `mileage-rate`, 2026; verify)
31 northwind owes noor due 30d ^inv-nw-2601
     ^inv-nw-2601[HR] @ 140.00 USD/HR #research                    // 38.5 HR worked in the month, from the `worked` lines
   // ▸ funded budget: 30% of the 9,540.00 that arrived in January = 2,862.00 USD moves checking -> savings, held for the tax reserve

31 checking = 9_704.55 USD
31 savings = 12_462.00 USD                                         // ▸ the reserve for taxes is the tied part of it

