// ═════ what Axiom derives on 2026-06-30 ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ▸ axiom tax 2026 --for noor (to date; cash)                                  Schedule C, by purpose
//   receipts 76,665.00  (retainer 28_425.00 · northwind 31_500.00 · kestrel 9_000.00 · devconf 7_740.00)
//   expenses 9,098.40  (rent share 1_404.00 · coworking 1_500.00 · software 774.00 · phone 162.00 · laptop 2_299.00 · accounting 400.00
//                    liability insurance 780.00 · business travel 1_240.00 · mileage 539.40 for 744 mi)
//   net profit 67,566.60 · self-employment tax 9,546.86 (15.3% of 92.35%) · adjustments: half of it 4,773.43, the premium 3_240.00, the solo 401(k) 9_000.00 -> AGI 50,553.17
//   QBI deduction 10,110.63 (20%) · standard deduction 16_100.00 · taxable 24,342.54 · income tax 2,673.10
//   solo 401(k) deferrals 9_000.00 of 24_500.00 · estimated tax paid for 2026 13_600.00 (6_800.00 on 04-15 and 06-15)
// ▸ axiom check
//   note[safe-harbor]: 2026's estimates so far are 13_600.00; 110% of 2025's tax is 27_200.00: on pace for the safe harbor
//   note[home-office]: 12% of rent and utilities is the business's; the simplified method would give 600.00: the actual method wins
//   note[reserve]: the tax reserve holds 22_999.50; income tax 2,673.10 and self-employment tax 9,546.86 on this half-year's profit are 12,219.96: the reserve covers it, with 2026's second half still to come

// ═════ index of marks ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//   fl-b04  ✎     [open]   a cost billed back at cost is income and spending at once; the purpose of the line is income
//   fl-b06  ✎     [A6]     the January installment belongs to the year before: `for the tax year`
//   fl-b07  ✎     [open]   budgets "of income" lost their root when §6.3 dropped `#income`; the funded reserve needs a word for "everything that arrived"
//   fl-c01  ✗     [A3]     a retainer is a claim on the client from the day it is invoiced, not only once a due day is missed (v4 §7); an `engagement` relator issues it
//   fl-c05  ✗     [open]   two bases again: expensing a laptop for tax (§179) against five years for the books
//   fl-s20  ⇄     [sync]   a time tracker's days as `worked` lines; the invoice then bills the sum by its code
//   fl-u02  ?     [A1]     a sole proprietor is both employer and participant of her own plan: one entity in two slots of one relator
